From 7e6638c36db962b0454f249e2b5ad8397c6ef434 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 22:44:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): drop pr-monitor concurrency group; reconcile sticky
 to exactly one (97e6a146)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rework of the Fix-1 red-X close after review. cancel-in-progress:false does NOT
stop cancellations: GitHub's queue replacement cancels a group's previously-PENDING
run UNCONDITIONALLY, and this workflow bursts (check_suite:completed fires ~10+/push),
so a group still left CANCELLED (red) runs. Remove the concurrency group entirely so
nothing is ever cancelled.

The only race a group guarded — two concurrent first-runs each CREATE a sticky comment
(the upsert was find-else-create) — is now closed deterministically: new
lib/pr-monitor/upsert-sticky.js reconciles to EXACTLY ONE by keeping the lowest-id
marker comment, updating it, and deleting the rest; a create landing after re-list
self-heals on the next event. Reconcile logic is unit-tested incl. a "comment appeared
between list and create" race; a test also asserts the workflow has no concurrency key.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
